             DSP routing is done by /vendor/bin/a6l-audio-route (libaudioroute + /vendor/etc/mixer_paths_a6l.xml),
             which follows the "Headphone Jack"/"Mic Jack" kcontrols of the card.
             r5 review F7 (28 Sep 2026): Earpiece exposed (in-call "voice-handset"; physically broken on Pierre's unit
             only) so that Telecom offers earpiece/speaker. Calls use the legacy policy routing of the primary output
             (no Telephony Rx/Tx devices); the HAL (tree patch audio/patches/0002) publishes the chosen call device in
             vendor.a6l.audio.call_out, which a6l-audio-route (codec/TFA paths) and a6l-q6voiced (DSP voice RX port:
             speaker = TERT_MI2S_RX / TFA9894) follow. -->
        <module name="primary" halVersion="3.0">
            <attachedDevices>
                <item>Earpiece</item>
                <item>Speaker</item>
                <item>Built-In Mic</item>
                <!-- btcall: modem call audio as devices (bridge policy) -->
                <item>Telephony Tx</item>
