        <!-- bt-audio (29 Sep 2026, docs/android-bt-audio-20260929.md): software data paths only (no DSP/SoC BT audio on the
             mainline q6 stack). A2DP: "a2dp output" -> BluetoothAudio provider (created in this HAL process by
             ModuleBluetooth) -> BT stack SBC/AAC/LDAC encoder -> HCI ACL. HFP/SCO: bluetooth.sco.managed_by_audio=true +
             bluetooth.hfp.software_datapath.enabled=true (audio/bluetooth/bt-audio.mk): the SCO devices below open
             HFP_SOFTWARE_{EN,DE}CODING_DATAPATH sessions and the stack carries the PCM (CVSD) / mSBC / LC3 frames over HCI
             SCO on the UART (WCN3990 has no usable PCM/slimbus link to the ADSP here). SCO mix ports are dynamic: the
             profile (8/16/32 kHz mono 16 bit) comes from the negotiated codec at connection. Cellular calls stay on the
